|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-42094" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6630ead363435c06aba0bc20398941c8f11be072358418b2a2f03a1ec15b01a2"} {"question" "q-42094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-42094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] ["math" "|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-42094" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using cofactor expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{21}+5\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+5|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-3-0)+5(-6-4) \\\\  & =3-50 \\\\  & =-47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+1\\cdot {C}_{22}+5\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(0-2)-5(-8-4) \\\\  & =-2+60 \\\\  & =58\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|=-47+58=11.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6630ead363435c06aba0bc20398941c8f11be072358418b2a2f03a1ec15b01a2"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-52"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "21"] ["math" "25"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+2\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+0\\cdot {C}_{24} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)(-15-32) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-47) \\\\  & =47\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 47=94.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77491" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6630ead363435c06aba0bc20398941c8f11be072358418b2a2f03a1ec15b01a2"} {"question" "q-77491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "24"] ["math" "42"] ["math" "49"] ["math" "92"] ["math" "94"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-77491" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "94"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14049356/state.json" "file_sha256" "cecffe9cbe29609acab7907b21f17046a8285988a65905edddfae640905a3ce3"} {"question" "q-130092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/